        "Helen H. Hobbs",
        "Jonathan C. Cohen",
        "Nabil G. Seidah"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "PCSK9 human genetics provided compelling target validation for a major new strategy to lower LDL cholesterol and prevent cardiovascular disease.",
        "attribution": "Hobbs and Cohen were central to the human-genetic evidence, and Seidah to the molecular identification of PCSK9.",
        "maturity": "The genetic mechanism and therapeutic value of PCSK9 inhibition have been strongly confirmed in clinical use.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The evidence supplied identifies several additional contributors whose relative claims require careful comparison.",
          "Recognition must distinguish discovery of the target from later drug development."
        ]
      }
    },
