      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optogenetics introduced a transformative way to test causal functions of genetically specified cells and has reshaped experimental neuroscience and physiology.",
        "attribution": "Bamberg and Nagel are central to channelrhodopsin characterization, while Deisseroth was pivotal in establishing the method as a broadly usable biological tool.",
        "maturity": "The approach is deeply established across laboratories and has produced extensive mechanistic insight.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The foundational work spans microbial photoreceptors, engineering, and in vivo application, creating difficult three-person attribution choices.",
          "Clinical application remains more limited than experimental impact."
        ]
      }
